/E (Dropping all missing readings is simple and takes O\(n\) time, but it may bias daily averages if missingness is systematic. Forward fill also takes O\(n\) time in one pass and uses O\(1\) extra state per station when rows are ordered by station and time. Median filling generally requires finding or sorting values; sorting takes O\(n log n\) time and O\(n\) storage in a straightforward implementation. The chosen strategy should preserve missingness information and document imputation.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [22]
>>
