/P 91 0 R
/E (Computing daily summaries in Python loops requires O\(n\) time and dictionary storage proportional to the number of station-day groups g. SQL aggregation also processes the n rows, typically O\(n\) without sorting/index effects, and returns only g summary rows. The database approach reduces data transfer and keeps the summary logic close to the stored data.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [20]
>>
