336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (A word-list scorer processes t tokens in O\(t\) time and uses O\(v\) storage for a vocabulary of size v. A trained model has model-loading memory overhead and inference cost depending on model size and input length. The simple rule-based solution is fast, transparent and suitable as a baseline for a small system; a trained model should be considered only after collecting representative labelled complaints and measuring accuracy.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
